# Keep Display Logic in State, Not in the Widget

**Rule:** Functions that format data or compute a display/fallback value belong in the `State` (or Model/Entity) as getters, not as helper methods inside the Widget. A widget's only job is to build the UI tree. This keeps the UI file "dumb" and centralizes display logic in one place.

### ❌ Bad Example
```dart
class MyWidget extends StatelessWidget {
  String _displayName(MyState state) => state.selectedItem?.name ?? 'Not selected';

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => BlocBuilder<MyCubit, MyState>(
        builder: (_, state) => Text(_displayName(state)),
      );
}
```

### ✅ Good Example
```dart
class MyState extends Equatable {
  final ItemEntity? selectedItem;
  String get displayName => selectedItem?.name ?? 'Not selected';
}

class MyWidget extends StatelessWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => BlocBuilder<MyCubit, MyState>(
        builder: (_, state) => Text(state.displayName),
      );
}
```
